  <h2>What the Music Player Offers</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Load files and folders:</strong> drop single tracks or entire folders, pick them via the buttons, or paste with Ctrl+V. A folder is taken over as a complete playlist.</li>
    <li><strong>Playlist management:</strong> the bar at the bottom shows the current track and its position in the list, such as "Track 3 of 25". Previous and next jump through the collection.</li>
    <li><strong>Shuffle and repeat:</strong> random order for variety, repeat for continuous playback at a party or while working.</li>
    <li><strong>Visualizer:</strong> an LED equalizer reacts live to the music. The dropdown offers further display modes, and a slider next to it adjusts the display.</li>
    <li><strong>Transport and volume:</strong> play, pause, stop, a progress bar with elapsed and remaining time, plus a volume slider with mute.</li>
    <li><strong>Formats:</strong> all common audio formats your browser can play, including MP3, WAV, OGG, FLAC and M4A.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Step by Step: Playing Music in the Browser</h2>

  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <div class="step-content">
        <strong>Open the Music Player</strong>
        <p>Go to <a href="https://kodinitools.com/ultimativer-musikplayer/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">kodinitools.com/ultimativer-musikplayer</a> — free, no registration.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="step-content">
        <strong>Add files or a folder</strong>
        <p>Drag music into the dashed area or click "Select Files" or "Select Folder". The tracks appear in the playlist immediately and the first one starts.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="step-content">
        <strong>Control playback</strong>
        <p>Use the buttons in the bar at the bottom to pause, stop or skip to the next track. Click the progress bar to jump within a track.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="step-content">
        <strong>Enable shuffle or repeat</strong>
        <p>The two outer buttons of the transport group toggle random playback and repeat.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="step-content">
        <strong>Adjust the visualizer</strong>
        <p>Below the visualizer, choose the mode in the dropdown and fine-tune the display with the slider.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="tip-box">
    <p><strong>Tip for large collections:</strong> keep your music in subfolders by genre or mood. One folder per occasion, loaded via "Select Folder", replaces assembling a playlist by hand. If you need playlists as files, the <a href="/en/blog/create-playlist-m3u/">Playlist Generator</a> is the right tool.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>When a Browser Player Is the Better Choice</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Someone else's computer:</strong> play music from a USB stick or download folder at the office, at school or at a friend's place without installing anything.</li>
    <li><strong>Background music:</strong> a tab with the player runs alongside your work without a separate app taking up resources.</li>
    <li><strong>Parties and events:</strong> load a folder, turn on shuffle and repeat, put the visualizer on the projector.</li>
    <li><strong>Quick preview:</strong> check downloads, recordings or exports from other KodiniTools right away.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Privacy: Music Stays on Your Device</h2>

  <p>
    The player reads files directly in the browser; nothing is uploaded. Neither tracks nor file names leave your computer. The same applies to the visualizer, which analyzes the audio locally via the Web Audio API.
  </p>

